# Feature 4: CI/CD Pipeline - COMPLETED

## Summary
Successfully implemented the CI/CD Pipeline for LedgerLens following the implementation plan in docs/implementation-plan/00-project-foundation/04-ci-cd-pipeline.md

## Files Created

### 1. `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
Main CI workflow that runs on push/PR to main:
- Matrix build for ubuntu-latest, macos-latest, windows-latest
- JDK 17 with temurin distribution
- Gradle caching with cache-read-only for non-main branches
- Runs `./gradlew check` for all checks
- Builds shared module and desktop app
- Uploads test results as artifacts

### 2. `.github/workflows/release.yml`
Release workflow triggered on version tags (v*):
- Android release APK with keystore secrets
- Desktop installers (DMG for macOS, MSI for Windows, DEB for Linux)
- Creates GitHub release with all artifacts

### 3. `.github/dependabot.yml`
Dependabot configuration:
- Gradle dependencies: weekly updates, max 5 PRs
- GitHub Actions: weekly updates

### 4. `.github/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md`
Documentation for branch protection rules including:
- Required PR reviews (1 approval)
- Required status checks (all CI jobs)
- Linear history enforcement
- Required secrets documentation for Android signing

## Acceptance Criteria Met
- [x] CI workflow runs on push and PR
- [x] All platform builds configured in CI
- [x] Tests run and report results (artifacts uploaded)
- [x] Lint checks (ktlint/detekt) gate PRs
- [x] Release workflow creates artifacts
- [x] Dependabot configured
- [x] Branch protection rules documented

## Required Secrets (for releases)
| Secret | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `KEYSTORE_BASE64` | Base64-encoded Android keystore |
| `KEYSTORE_PASSWORD` | Keystore password |
| `KEY_ALIAS` | Signing key alias |
| `KEY_PASSWORD` | Key password |
